    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the circle with centre $(3,-4)$ passing through the origin.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x-3)^2+(y+4)^2=25$",
      "worked": "The radius is the distance from $(3,-4)$ to $(0,0)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}r^2&=(0-3)^2+(0-(-4))^2\\\\r^2&=9+16\\\\r^2&=25\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)^2+(y-(-4))^2&=25\\\\(x-3)^2+(y+4)^2&=25\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
